* DEFINE registers FACT with parameter N and a matching FACT entry label.
* LE(N,1) succeeds at the base case and :S(BASE) skips the recursive call.
* Each invocation has its own parameter binding. RETURN yields the value assigned to FACT.
    DEFINE('FACT(N)')
    OUTPUT = FACT(4) :(END)
FACT LE(N,1) :S(BASE)
    FACT = N * FACT(N - 1) :(RETURN)
BASE FACT = 1 :(RETURN)
END
